PR159_PHYSICAL_FINDING_3_CORRECTION

Correction to the earlier physical interpretation.

The observed browser state on head 3ef25ab771178ef22f38a30a0ae260ceb41f6200 was NOT a partial prompt send.

After comparing the complete rendered user turn with the complete text still present in the composer, the actual physical failure was:

- the full WORKER_TASK_V1 prompt was submitted and rendered as one complete user turn;
- the full same WORKER_TASK_V1 prompt remained in the composer after that successful Send;
- therefore the provider failed to clear the composer after Send, leaving a complete duplicate visually ready for accidental re-send.

Corrected failure class:
A provider may successfully submit the complete task while retaining an exact duplicate of that task in the live composer. Delivery correlation alone is therefore insufficient to prove the browser UI is disarmed against an accidental duplicate Send.

Corrected closure on current HEAD be4102493d96d00b9b2b4e92ff4cc047b39a2a17:
- remove the speculative pre-Send 2-second stability delay because it addressed the wrong mechanism;
- after exactly one physical Send, require the correlated full user turn;
- if the composer still contains exactly the same full prompt, clear that exact duplicate locally without clicking Send again;
- only after the composer is proven empty may delivery become `delivered`;
- if non-empty composer content is not the exact full duplicate, do not clear it and fail closed to `unknown` after the bounded observation window;
- no second Send path is introduced.

